%N A125928 Sprague-Grundy values for octal game .7007.
%C A125928 Octal game .7037 also has values a(n). Octal games 4.004, 4.006, 4.014, 4.016, 4.204, 4.206, 4.214 and 4.216 have values a(n-1).
%C A125928 a(n) is also the Sprague-Grundy value of a heap of n+1 tokens in the octal game 4.004; equivalently, the Sprague-Grundy sequence of 4.004 is 0, 0, followed by this sequence. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Aug 05 2026
%C A125928 Computed (as the game 4.004) through heap size 2^30 = 1073741824 by Tyler Satchel Orden (2026), extending A. Flammenkamp's tables for 4.004, which reached 2^28. All of Flammenkamp's published invariants at 2^28 (8914 rare values in his sparse-space sense, last at heap size 43090760; maximum value 1996, first at heap size 20532406) were reproduced exactly before extending. No new rare value appears through 2^30 and the maximum value is unchanged. - _Tyler Satchel Orden_, Aug 05 2026
%D A125928 E. R. Berlekamp, J. H. Conway and R. K. Guy, Winning Ways, Academic Press, NY, 2 vols., 1982; see Chapter 4, p. 104.
